DESCRIPTION
Whenever I try to remove any object from the Global Environment/Workspace, the
RKWard GUI instantly crashes with a Segmentation fault (core dumped). The
backend successfully executes the `rm()` command and performs an emergency
save, but the frontend crashes when trying to update the object model.

STEPS TO REPRODUCE
1. Open RKWard using the official Linux AppImage.
2. Create any object in the R Console (e.g., `anova.results <- 1`).
3. Delete the object (e.g., running `rm(anova.results)` or deleting it via the
Workspace Browser GUI). 

OBSERVED RESULT
RKWard crashes immediately. Terminal shows: `Violación de segmento ('core'
generado)` (Segmentation fault).

EXPECTED RESULT
The object is removed and the Workspace Browser updates without crashing.

SOFTWARE/OS VERSIONS
Operating System (available in the Info Center app, or by running `kinfo` in a
terminal window):
KDE Plasma Version: 
KDE Frameworks Version: 
Qt Version: 

ADDITIONAL INFORMATION
I ran the AppImage with `--debug-level 5`. The logs clearly point to an
assertion failure in the UI model update logic.

Here is the crucial part of the **Frontend trace**:
```text
Trace: /builds/education/rkward/src/rkward/core/rkmodificationtracker.cpp -
function index line 266
Trace: /builds/education/rkward/src/rkward/core/robject.cpp - function
numChildrenForObjectModel line 573
Trace: /builds/education/rkward/src/rkward/core/rcontainerobject.cpp - function
numChildren line 201
Assert 'row < parent_object->numChildrenForObjectModel()' failed at
/builds/education/rkward/src/rkward/core/rkmodificationtracker.cpp - function
index line 277
```

Here is the corresponding **Backend trace** right before the crash, showing the
backend finishes the removal and the frontend disconnects:
```text
B 68720747: done running command remove (anova.results), status: 2
B 68720747: Trace: /builds/education/rkward/src/rkward/rbackend/rkrbackend.cpp
- function checkObjectUpdatesNeeded line 1601
B 68720747: removed anova.results
B 68724630: Trace:
/builds/education/rkward/src/rkward/rbackend/rktransmitter.cpp - function
disconnected line 254
B 68724630: Transmission error Connection closed unexpectedly. Last error was:
QLocalSocket: Remote closed
B 68729167: Created emergency save file in
/home/cano/.rkward/rkward_recover0.RData
```

